sn35.229:3.1 starts: “One who has expunged lust and hate
sn35.229:3.2 starts: Along with the taint of ignorance,
sn35.229:3.3 starts: Has crossed this ocean so hard to cross
sn35.229:3.4 starts: With its dangers of sharks, demons, waves.
sn35.95:24.1 starts: “When, firmly mindful, one sees a form,
sn35.95:24.2 starts: One is not inflamed by lust for forms;
sn35.95:24.3 starts: One experiences it with dispassionate mind
sn35.95:24.4 starts: And does not remain holding it tightly.
sn35.95:25.1 starts: “One fares mindfully in such a way
sn35.95:25.2 starts: That even as one sees the form,
sn35.95:25.3 starts: And while one undergoes a feeling,
sn35.95:25.4 starts: Suffering is exhausted, not built up.
sn35.95:25.5 starts: For one dismantling suffering thus,
sn35.95:25.6 starts: Nibbāna is said to be close by.
sn36.1:2.1 starts: A disciple of the Buddha, mindful,
sn36.1:2.2 starts: Concentrated, comprehending clearly,
sn36.1:2.3 starts: Understands feelings
sn36.1:2.4 starts: And the origin of feelings,
sn36.2:2.1 starts: Whether it be pleasant or painful
sn36.2:2.2 starts: Along with the neither-painful-nor-pleasant,
sn36.2:2.3 starts: Both the internal and the external,
sn36.2:2.4 starts: Whatever kind of feeling there is:
